        <h1>
          How Receipt works
        </h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Scan a paper receipt, get stock in the shop you bought from. This page covers
          <em>          what pays, how much, and when it arrives
</em>
          .
        </p>
        <section id="what">
          <h2>
            What Receipt is
          </h2>
          <p>
            You photograph a paper receipt. We read the merchant, the date and the total, and check that it is a genuine, unclaimed receipt. If it qualifies, we set aside a reward in the stock of the brand you bought from.
          </p>
          <p>
            Rewards are fractional tokenized shares of the merchant, funded from $RECEIPT trading fees. Holding $RECEIPT raises what each receipt pays you — that is the tier ladder below.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="flow">
          <h2>
            How a scan becomes stock
          </h2>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <strong>              Scan
</strong>
              — photograph the receipt in the app.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>              Read
</strong>
              — we extract the merchant, date and total.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>              Check
</strong>
              — we confirm the receipt is genuine and has not been claimed before.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>              Reserve
</strong>
              — your reward is set aside and appears in your app straight away.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>              Deliver
</strong>
              — the stock tokens are transferred to your wallet.
            </li>
          </ol>
          <div class="note">
            <span class="lb">            Reserved, then delivered
</span>
            <p>
              A reward shows in your app the moment it is approved, before it moves on-chain. A reservation is a promise we keep.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
