        <section id="price">
          <h2>
            How your tier is decided
          </h2>
          <p>
            We read your $RECEIPT balance and value it in dollars at the market price.
          </p>
          <h3 id="hw-h">
            When your tier changes
          </h3>
          <!-- Written from the server's setting rather than promising a rule it
           may not be applying: the 24-hour high-water window is off, and a
           dip does drop a tier. Only a live lock holds a price. -->
          <p id="hw-p">
            Your tier is whatever your $RECEIPT is worth right now, at the market price. Buy more and you move up immediately; if the price falls or you sell, you move down the same way. Nothing is held back or averaged. The one thing that holds a price is a
            <a href="/lock">            lock
</a>
            : locked tokens count at the price you locked at or today&#39;s, whichever is higher, for the whole term.
          </p>
          <div class="note">
            <span class="lb">            Always in your favour
</span>
            <p>
              If we cannot read a price at all, everyone earns the Paper rate. A problem on our side can never pay you less than the base rate.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section id="rule">
          <h2>
            What a receipt pays
          </h2>
          <h3>
            One rule, and this is all of it
          </h3>
          <p>
            A receipt pays
            <strong>            your tier’s percentage of its total
</strong>
            , capped by whatever is left of your day. Nothing else takes part: no welcome bonus, no full match, and no minimum.
          </p>
          <p>
            At Gold’s 3%, a $50 shop pays $1.50 and a $158 shop pays $4.75. Once the day’s cap is reached, further receipts wait for tomorrow.
          </p>
          <h3>
            There is no minimum
          </h3>
          <p>
            A receipt is worth its rate, however small — a $2.31 coffee at Black’s 5% pays 11¢. Small receipts are paid rather than refused, which is what a minimum used to do to the tail of every day.
          </p>
          <div class="note">
            <span class="lb">            Rounding
</span>
            <p>
              Every calculation is done in whole cents, and rounding never works against you.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
