            Delivery
          </h2>
          <p>
            An approved reward is reserved right away and visible in your app. Delivery moves the tokens to your wallet on-chain.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Your reward is shown as
              <strong>              reserved
</strong>
              until it is sent, then
              <strong>              delivered
</strong>
              once the chain confirms it.
            </li>
            <li>
              Each reward is delivered once and only once.
            </li>
            <li>
              If a delivery does not go through, it is held for a person to check rather than retried automatically.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The profile bonus is the exception: it is held for 7 days before delivery.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="onchain">
          <h2>
            On-chain receipts
          </h2>
          <p>
            A swap on a decentralised exchange is already a receipt: public, unforgeable and impossible to reuse. Where this feature is enabled, you can connect a Solana wallet and claim recent swaps the same way you would a paper receipt.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Connect and sign for your Solana wallet, and your recent swaps become claimable.
            </li>
            <li>
              What you spent on the swap is the receipt total.
            </li>
            <li>
              Swaps of very thinly traded tokens do not qualify.
            </li>
            <li>
              The same rules apply as a paper receipt: age, size, three a day, the first-receipt match and your tier’s limits.
            </li>
            <li>
              The reward is paid in the token you bought. Each swap can be claimed once, ever.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section id="fair">
          <h2>
            Keeping it fair
          </h2>
          <p>
            The rewards pool is shared, so every receipt has to be a real purchase by a real person.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>              One purchase, one reward.
</strong>
              Each receipt pays exactly once, no matter who scans it or how it is photographed.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>              Genuine receipts only.
</strong>
              We check for edited images, screenshots and reprints. Submitting a receipt that is not yours, or altering one, can cost you access.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>              People, not just software.
</strong>
              Anything unusual is reviewed by a person before it is refused or approved.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Scanning your own receipts, from your own purchases, is all that is ever asked.
          </p>
        </section>
